  partName: Spark Plug (3)
  description: The Spark Plug (3) is a third spark plug located at the top-center-front
    of the engine, responsible for igniting the fuel-air mixture in another combustion
    chamber. Made of Material.001, this tiny, complex-shaped part plays a critical
    role in the engine's operation, and its precise positioning ensures efficient
    combustion. Interestingly, the spark plug's complex shape allows for optimal
    spark formation and propagation, even in high-temperature and high-pressure environments.
